 "summary": "Phospholipase A₂ frees arachidonic acid from membrane phospholipids (blocked indirectly by glucocorticoids). Cyclooxygenase (COX-1/2; NSAIDs, aspirin) makes PGH₂, which becomes thromboxane A₂ (platelets: aggregation, vasoconstriction), prostacyclin (endothelium: anti-aggregation, vasodilation) and prostaglandins (PGE₂: fever, pain, vasodilation, ductus arteriosus). 5-Lipoxygenase (zileuton) makes leukotrienes: LTB₄ draws neutrophils; LTC₄, D₄, E₄ constrict bronchi (montelukast and zafirlukast block their receptor).",
